/**
 * The `position-anchor` [CSS](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS) property specifies
 * the default anchor element for a positioned element. This default is used by `position-area` and
 * `position-try`, and by anchor functions (`anchor()` and `anchor-size()`) when no `<anchor-name>`
 * argument is provided to those functions.
 *
 * Initial: normal. Inherited: no.
 * Percentages: not accepted.
 *
 * Keyword effects:
 * - auto: Associates a positioned element with its implicit anchor element, if it has one — for
 * example as set by the non-standard HTML
 * [`anchor`](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/HTML/Reference/Global_attributes/anchor)
 * attribute.
 * - match-parent: Uses the same default anchor element as the parent element, or the originating
 * element if this is a
 * [pseudo-element](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Glossary/Pseudo-element), provided that
 * would be an acceptable anchor element (that is [part of the
 * tree](https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Selectors/Pseudo-elements#tree-abiding_pseudo-elements)).
 * Otherwise, it has no default anchor element.
 * - none: The positioned element is not associated with an anchor element.
 * - normal: If `position-area` is `none`, it behaves as `none`. Otherwise it behaves as `auto`.
 *
 * Grammar: normal | none | auto | <anchor-name> | match-parent
 *
 * Specification: https://drafts.csswg.org/css-anchor-position-1/#propdef-position-anchor
 *
 * Author guide:
 * https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/position-anchor
